					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/psul" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2156983); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2156983&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606373947" alt="psul" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2156983)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/psul" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2156983); return false;" >psul</a></span> <span class="odate time_1495626351 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">24 May 2017 11:45</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2831072">
									

<p>There is no real structure here. It feels like you have put in a smorgasbord of standard SCP elements - recovery, mysterious note, breach procedure, doctors' notes, interview log and experiment logs - without having a real purpose or literary goal. SCPs don't need to be stories - sometimes the convenience of documents just happening to form a narrative is distracting - but I much prefer them when they have a point. This just sits there without bringing much to the table other than the picture.</p>
<p>As a side note, how can an audio log include details such as:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>visibly anxious</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>looks grave</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>shuffles uncomfortably</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>looks grave [again!]</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>[Shivering.]</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>places his head in his hands</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>leaning forward in his seat</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>stares for a second or two, leaning back in his chair</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>shows visible signs of distress</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>now standing, gradually sits back down. Trembling.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Edit: video / audio - easy things to confuse, even for me!</p>

							</div>

								
